From 10c6f6c684d0462c04953a36af956ed9e342811c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:24:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: don't bypass the bridge on an unused
 path

nft_dev_forward_path() stores the output device of the discovered
forward path even when the path is not used afterwards because its input
device is not part of the flowtable.  The flow then stays on
FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH, and that transmit path looks the output device
up by the stored interface index.  Behind a bridge this is the bridge
port, so the packets are sent straight out of the port with the next hop
resolved on the bridge, skipping the bridge's own egress handling.  A DSA
switch tagger that uses a port's standalone VLAN for such frames then
gets them dropped by the switch, and every routed flow towards the LAN
stalls as soon as it is offloaded.

Only use the output device of the path when the path is used, and
transmit on the dst device otherwise.  The output device is never NULL
when the input device is set, as nft_dev_path_info() falls back to the
input device.

Mainline avoids the problem differently: since commit 871df5007eda
("netfilter: flowtable: bail out if forward path cannot be
discovered") such flows are not offloaded at all.

Signed-off-by: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
@@ -203,13 +203,14 @@ static void nft_dev_forward_path(struct nf_flow_route *route,
 	if (nft_dev_fill_forward_path(route, dst, ct, dir, ha, &stack) >= 0)
 		nft_dev_path_info(&stack, &info, ha, &ft->data);
 
-	if (info.outdev)
-		route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex = info.outdev->ifindex;
-	else
+	/* A path that is not used leaves the flow on XMIT_NEIGH, which must
+	 * go out through the dst device and not a lower device of it.
+	 */
+	if (!info.indev || !nft_flowtable_find_dev(info.indev, ft)) {
 		route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex = dst->dev->ifindex;
-
-	if (!info.indev || !nft_flowtable_find_dev(info.indev, ft))
 		return;
+	}
+	route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex = info.outdev->ifindex;
 
 	route->tuple[!dir].in.ifindex = info.indev->ifindex;
 	for (i = 0; i < info.num_encaps; i++) {
